A||N||10||Fiero_Freak||Body Identification plate?||||4||
Z||000000||Fiero_Freak||10-20-2000||02:55 PM||||Does anyone know where this thing is.  I bought a parts car...and possible kit.  I need to title it. This form needs to be filled out and it asks for the Vehicle VIN, Police VIN (I'm guessing the body number, and the Engine VIN.   I'm pretty sure the engine VIN is on the side of the head.   Just can't find this other plate.  The factory manual says it's behind the headlight in the engine compartment.  Literally, that puts is somewhere between the front and the back of the car.   If anyone could help I would appreciate it.||||reg||4
Z||000001||Raydar||10-20-2000||03:13 PM||||There is a 4" x 5" sticker on the inside of the trunk, on the left front wheelwell. Contains all the RPO codes. <BR>Think that might be the one they refer to? <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_Freak||10-20-2000||03:24 PM||||  I think there is something else.  I've seen these on other cars.  They are accually metal and rivited to the car.  I've looked around and it's nowhere obvious..at least not that I've seen.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||10-20-2000||05:08 PM||||I think it's riveted to the wall that the headlights bolt to.<P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||dman||10-20-2000||06:23 PM||||Hello everyone. Try this, remove the drivers side front speaker grill on top of the dash, then remove the speaker (this really isn't all that hard to do!), you should be able to see a small plate riveted on the metal dash frame. This has a copy of the VIN stamped on it. Of course the normal VIN should be visible on top of the dash, right where it meets the windshield so this other plate really isn't that necessary unless you lost the main VIN plate somehow.<P>Hmm...I think you can see it using that method, otherwise you need to remove the dash.<P>There are other places on the frame with numbers stamped onto it. Which number you're asking for I don't really know. Hope this helped.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Necromancer||10-20-2000||06:55 PM||||The plate is located on the driver's side of the car, on the 'wall' between the headlight cubbyhole and the spare tire space, facing the rear of the car. It right near the the opening where the front wiring harness comes through.<P>I've added a picture on my website.  <A HREF="http://www.borg.com/~necro/pix/fierobp.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.borg.com/~necro/pix/fierobp.jpg</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Necromancer (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero_Freak||10-22-2000||01:49 AM||||Damn...  I didn't think I would miss it there.  I looked and I just don't have one.  Have the flat space, just no plate.  On either side.  I have the front just about as stripped as yours.  ????  I'm at a loss.  I can see the regular vin... on the dash... no problem.  They just want to see the body plate.  I cannot think of any other locations.  Thanks for all the help...and if you have any other ideas I would appreciate them.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||10-22-2000||10:09 AM||||As I recall from the olden days, the term 'body plate' only contained the vehicle identification number, hince the term VIN.<BR>I fear that your on a wild goose chase!||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||10-22-2000||10:49 AM||||The LEGAL ID or VIN number is the one on dash visible thru bottom of windshield. Its the only one that DMV, local, state, federal agencies/police recognize. If they want another ID plate, make them find it, its there job-not yours. If its been removed, could have been because the vehicle was totalled. Insurance companies sometimes remove them so it cant be resold or tagged again-keeps crooks from repairing it and selling it to an unsuspecting buyer.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero_Freak||10-22-2000||12:41 PM||||That could be very possible... but it doesn't look like anything has been there.  I thought they were riveted to the body.  The only problem is, if they have to look for it.  They want to do it at the Highway patrol inspection station.  It's going to be pretty hard to get it there without the cradle in it.  I wasn't going to pull the tranny and such, just the motor.  Just to not piss them off I wanted to do their work so I could get this done as fast as possible.  Thanks again for all your help.<P>Dana Mitchell||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||10-22-2000||03:40 PM||||According to the Haynes manual-"The body number plate is located in the front compartment attached to the front tie bar behind either the left or right headlamp."<BR>FWIW||||reg||1
